within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EC03_Encorafenib;
model Encorafenib_Yang2026_PD_aenz
  "indirect_response_iii exposure-response sweep — Yang_2026 :: AENZ (enzyme amount)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 1,      // [1]
    Emax = 1.861,  // type III effect term
    EC50 = 9.097e-06,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 + Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type III
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 91, Interval = 0.182),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Encorafenib_Yang2026_PD_aenz</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Yang DZ et al., <i>Clinical pharmacokinetics 65(5):693–707</i> 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40262-025-01608-y\">doi:10.1007/s40262-025-01608-y</a>) — enzyme amount against encorafenib ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_iii.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =          1          drug-free response (baseline) (baseline enzyme amount ratio, Q324)
  Emax  =      1.861          maximal effect term (maximum autoinduction effect, Q320)
  EC50  =      9.097 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (concentration at half maximum effect, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 + Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of encorafenib per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 1   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (9.097 ng/mL)  response 1.93
  exposure -> infinity  response 2.861</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Yang_2026: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Encorafenib_Yang2026_PD_aenz;
